Coordination from the design-boards epic (bd-01M4R9BYCYAZAPHYSK79MVWHKW, owner-approved 2026-10-13): the Analysis editing tranche (expected-unmatched selection, S7.1-S7.4) should proceed. It implements what the 2026-10-11 Analysis board shows. Three conditions keep it consistent with the new UI:
1. Base on origin/main AFTER design batch 3 lands (gating now, candidate 8decd235; it changes ResolvedDesignView.scala and studio-design.css). Reserve files with mote. Slice S8 (bd-01M4R9D4N798K45G1RBT93QC1Z) is adding a shared studio-controls.css for RadioButton/CheckBox/Slider, and S9 (bd-01M4R9D5EFMMZ6R7ANBVX1PRQK) will add a SegmentedBar. Use those for preset radios, form controls and scale chips instead of styling controls locally.
2. Follow the rules that just landed (DESIGN_SPEC §15):
   - selected items use -es-sel-fill plus semibold (Sans SmBld; Mono Medm for mono text), never accent-soft;
   - focus rings use :focus-visible only;
   - a list or chip group is one Tab stop with a row-level cursor (CompositeFocus);
   - disabled controls attach their visible reason with DisabledReason.attach;
   - every string goes through text ids;
   - type sizes are 11/12/13/16/28 only, with the TypeCss helpers .t11-strong/.t12-strong/.t12-label/.mono-500;
   - colours come only from Tokens.
3. S7.4's protocol/exploratory scale labels are on neither the Analysis board nor in DESIGN_SPEC. Get a spec source (and a board edit if they are visible) before building them, or leave them out.
On landing: update the Analysis section of docs/studio/PARITY_CHECKLIST.md, and note that the board's "pending UI-A / UI-F" descriptor tags are replaced by served descriptors.
